      "To compare RSS with contemporary feeds without assuming a linear progression, I return to Instagram as documented in early 2022. In March, Meta introduced Following, a chronological view of posts from followed accounts, and Favorites, a chronological view from up to fifty selected accounts (Mosseri, 2022a). The standard Home feed, however, still combined followed accounts with suggested content, while Favorites posts could also be promoted within Home. This coexistence is analytically useful: one platform offered both explicitly selected streams and platform-organized visibility. Meta framed these options as ways to give people control, but a product announcement establishes available functions, not whether they increased news diversity or changed everyday habits. Instagram here is a bounded comparison of interface rules, not the inevitable successor to RSS.",
